Problem 4: Understanding How Deep the Boat Will Sit
A boat can float without necessarily having enough of its hull above the water.
Why it's difficult: A boat that technically floats might sit too low in the water to be practical or safe.
How your tool helps: Estimate the submerged portion of the hull and show the remaining height above the water.
You could display a simple illustration of a boat hull with a waterline.
Problem 5: Understanding the Effect of Added Cargo
Adding passengers or cargo increases the boat's total weight.
Why it's difficult: Users may not realize how quickly additional weight reduces the hull's remaining capacity.
How your tool helps: Include a passenger-and-cargo input and recalculate the result whenever the user changes the weight.
This feature would make the application interactive without requiring complicated programming.

